Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||02-14-2001||10:41 AM||||afew things...<P>1.for somereason I can't see any of the pics in your gallery, I get a java error when I try.<P>2.Your head unit is sticking out. I'm guessing you ran into the metal bracket in the back. there are 2 rivets holding it in place to a plastic panel. It's reletively easy to remove, w/ some elbow grease if you use a variaty of screw drivers to wedge under it and pop the rivets threw the plastic.<P>3. I can hardly stand the rearward visibility in my formula as is, I can't imagine blocking the whole rear window. Not to mention the legality issue of it. I don't know where you are, but in WI there are limits as to blocking your windows (front and rear) but as long as you don't hit anything, that's all you.<P>4. I don't like rap. :P but you're right about those dash speakers.<P>Nice job over all tho. One question... how tall are you?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by ThatRickGuy (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gasolene||02-14-2001||02:01 PM||||If you use older versions of netscape you will get java errors, I'm not sure why, I use ie5.5.<P>You don't need to see out the back window, side mirrors are fine if you know how to use them.  It takes a while to get used to, but after a couple weeks you don't even notice.  In alberta It's legal to block out back window as long as you have both side mirrors.<P>I don't like rap either, but rap and R&B music has alot of low frequency bass which sounds really nice.  rock music doesn't sound that great in my system as rock music has no really low bass.<P>I can e-mail u pics if you want.  I'm about 5'10. I lost an inch of leg room, but it was worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jch82||02-14-2001||02:09 PM||||Did you ever consider using plexiglass for the two subs in the back window? It would be more expensive but then you would have a chance of seeing out the back window. So what does it sound like having those subs right behind your ears? I would love to do that install but maybe with plexiglass whenever I get my fiero.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Before you criticize someone, walk a mile in his shoes. That way, if he  gets angry, he'll be a mile way - and barefoot....||||reg||5
Z||000009||Gasolene||02-14-2001||03:01 PM||||There was a error with the java gallery but it has now been fixed.  (I HATE Microsoft FRONTPAGE), but I don't have anything else.<P>the enclosure is expensive enough without plexiglass, I'm not sure If I would want wires visible in the window.  I'm fine without a back window, I don't even notice it.  It just takes time to get used to, like driving a new car for the first time.||||reg||1
