Z||000011||sqoach||02-14-2001||03:48 PM||||looks like you took a lot of time with this setup. i personally don't like it much. way too much bass. i mean come on, 4 subs. what the hell for? going deaf would be a reason i guess, but who would want that? my friend has 2 rockford 10s in his car and they hit like hell. you can hear the damn thing 3 blocks away. i swear he's already lost some hearing ability.<P>it's a nice clean setup though. just not for me since i want to be able to hear when i'm older.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||02-14-2001||05:13 PM||||How is that box in the window secured? Man, I'd be deathly afraid of someone hitting me and having that box rip my head off! Have you considered buying something that needs that much speaker, like, oh let's say, a BUS?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm with sqoach, impressive looking but way overkill.||||reg||5
Z||000013||Gasolene||02-14-2001||05:30 PM||||Of course it's overkill.  Why do you put a V8 in a fiero, Why do they make 1/2 million$ cars, does anyone really need a 14k gold watch.<BR>I love car audio, plus it's the only fiero in the world that I know of with 2 10's and 2 12's.  It's not for everyone, some people don't love car audio as much as I do.  I would never spend thousands on a painting. but some people do.<P>As for the box falling down, the top box is mounted to the bottom box, which is bolted to the floor.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club<p>[This message has been edited by Gasolene (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||sqoach||02-14-2001||05:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gasolene:<BR><B>Of course it's overkill.  Why do you put a V8 in a fiero, Why do they make 1/2 million$ cars, does anyone really need a 14k gold watch.<BR>I love car audio, plus it's the only fiero in the world that I know of with 2 10's and 2 12's.  It's not for everyone, some people don't love car audio as much as I do.  I would never spend thousands on a painting. but some people do.<P>As for the box falling down, the top box is mounted to the bottom box, which is bolted to the floor.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>answers to your questions:<BR>Why do you put a V8 in a fiero?<BR>i don't, but archie does  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Why do they make 1/2 million$ cars?<BR>so the filthy rich people can have something to drive.<P>does anyone really need a 14k gold watch?<BR>no, they need 24k gold watches  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>i guess everyone's got their own taste in something. and that's not a bad thing.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Homicidal||02-15-2001||03:44 AM||||Taken from website:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>frequencies above 80Hz produce a loud "buzzing" vibration inside the interior. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Dynomat bud.  LOTS of it, EXTREME quality too, not the regular crap.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I havn't had the S.P.L. tested yet, but when it's cranked, everything looks a bit blurry. Some people have told me it's hard to breath. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>That's..........SCARY.  <P>Guy at my work has a similiar setup, Mustang with 3 MTX Bkue Thunder 10's and one 10" Bazooka.  Impressive, even shakes the Circuit City sign at my work (where I work) from in the Parking Lot.  But sorry, much too much.  There is such a thing as too much bass.  <P>That's why I LOVE my 10" Sub in the front compartment, the bass sounds great, powerful and doesn't drown out any Mids or Highs like your setup would by letting just enough bass waves in the car!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>My stereo on mute, is louder than most typical car audio systems on max.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not to be a nit-pick, but that is a physical impossibility bro!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Impressive nonetheless.  Ever think of entering in the DB Dragraces?||||reg||1
Z||000016||Oreif||02-15-2001||10:38 AM||||I'll admit it is impressive with the sub set-up. But the only stereo contest you have a chance of winning is the SPL drag races.<BR>You'll lose many points on sound quality, tonal flatness, and installation. (they don't like it when you block windows and the head unit sticking out is not good, from their standpoint)<BR>As for the rest of the system, in order to compensate for the large volume of bass, your going to need a lot of mid-bass and mids to overcome the SPL of the subs.<BR>Also I'd be very careful who sits in the car when you crank it up. With the subs so close and the power you can actually stop a heart if the bass hits at the correct time.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Homicidal||02-15-2001||02:04 PM||||I'm curious, why have two 12's behind the seat?<P>With them behind the seat and absolutely no space between the seat and the sub, it fires directly into the seat, which gives off a muddy, muffled bass, doesn't it?<P>The two 10's compenstate for that though, it seems.<P>Personally, I would redesign it with 1 10" instead of 2 inside the cockpit and move one sub to the front trunk.  Would give a much better bass reproduction and a more well rounded sound overall.<p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Gasolene||02-15-2001||02:21 PM||||quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>My stereo on mute, is louder than most typical car audio systems on max.<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>When I mute my stereo, it lowers the volume by 50%.  (thats what I meant)<P>I also, initially thought that becasue the subs are pressed up against the seat that sound would be dampned and muffled.  But because the seat is not very dence, the sound passes through fine.  I notice NO difference between the seats back, and up.  However when another person sits in the car, there is a very noticable drop in volume.  (Humans are very dense, lots of H2O).  It also gives a unique sensation with the vibration right on your back.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club||||reg||1
Z||000019||Formula||02-15-2001||02:33 PM||||I sat in a blazer with 9 15" american bass vfls that hit 162 dbs......yeeeaaahhhhowww<P>and my friend has an eclipse with 4 mtx thunder 8000 15s.....lets put it this way, its hard to breathe AND you can see stop signs blur badly, and its only in the low 150s.<P>but personally, I really like my 1 10" Xplode in the front trunk, it sounds perfect!||||reg||1
Z||000020||Gasolene||02-15-2001||02:42 PM||||If I could fit 9 15' subwoofers in my Fiero, I would.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club||||reg||1
Z||000021||stimpy||02-15-2001||04:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gasolene:<BR><B>If I could fit 9 15' subwoofers in my Fiero, I would.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Easy solution. Go get yourself a Pontiac Trans Sport and put Fiero badges on it. Might as well, because by the time you add the weight of 9 15" subs, the amps to run em, the extra batteries to power the amps, and the enclosures to hold it all, you wouldn't have anything close to a sports car.  Really, I wouldn't be offended if you bought a Honda Civic Hatchback.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000022||DJRice||02-15-2001||08:07 PM||||How long did it take for your rearview mirror to fall off?<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000023||Homicidal||02-15-2001||10:58 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gasolene:<BR>[B]I also, initially thought that becasue the subs are pressed up against the seat that sound would be dampned and muffled. But because the seat is not very dence, the sound passes through fine. I notice NO difference between the seats back, and up. However when another person sits in the car, there is a very noticable drop in volume. (Humans are very dense, lots of H2O). It also gives a unique sensation with the vibration right on your back.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know, I had my 10" just like that.  It's absolutely horrible.  What DID help was to turn it around and had to fire towards the firewall, but put a 1" spacer in between the wall and the sub.  This created an almost "ported" like surrounding and was really cool.  Thing is, it was deafening with just 1 10", so I'm afraid of your car.<P>BTW, found the pounding fun at first and then increasingly HORRIBLE.  Especially after hearing it turned and then in the front trunk, much nicer!  Remember, bass is AIR and bass WAVES, not just rattling stuff.<P>Take my advice, get one up front!<BR>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 02-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Gasolene||02-16-2001||12:00 AM||||quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>I know, I had my 10" just like that. It's absolutely horrible.<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>The reason your sub sounded better facing back instead of front has nothing to do with the seat being in the way.  How the sound waves bounce off the interior walls of the car determines how it will sound.  Some subs and enclosures produce better sound pointed in different directions.<P>quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Remember, bass is AIR and bass WAVES, not just rattling stuff.<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>There is very little rattle in my car (of course some is to be expected, but its hardly noticable).  The sound that is produced by the subs is clean low pressure sound waves. especially when the windows and doors are open.<P>quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Take my advice, get one up front!<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Placing subwoofers behind and infront of you will produce sound waves that de-constructivly interfer with each other, dampening the sound.  Also, the sound waves loose some of their energy passing through the front ports in the front Fire Wall. (assuming you have ports)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club||||reg||1
Z||000025||Homicidal||02-16-2001||01:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gasolene:<BR>[quote]The reason your sub sounded better facing back instead of front has nothing to do with the seat being in the way. How the sound waves bounce off the interior walls of the car determines how it will sound. Some subs and enclosures produce better sound pointed in different directions.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>On the contrary, it has a large put to do with the bass quality.  Tell you what, find a sealed box of 2 12's inside and place them firing towards a big foam block and tell me the bass isn't reduced horribly.  There is no way those 12's can be doing any good besides just giving you an nice back massage.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Placing subwoofers behind and infront of you will produce sound waves that de-constructivly interfer with each other, dampening the sound. Also, the sound waves loose some of their energy passing through the front ports in the front Fire Wall. (assuming you have ports)<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your Fiero doesn't have a front firewall bro, that's in the rear.  Plus, I highly doubt they would interfere with each other unless you have them directly firing towards each other.<P>If you placed one 10" in the front trunk and then ported it into the cab, the front trunk creates a "hatchback" like effect off the trunk lid and if you ever heard a nice setup in a hatchback, this can be a very powerful tool!  ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Gasolene||02-16-2001||02:08 PM||||quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>On the contrary, it has a large put to do with the bass quality. Tell you what, find a sealed box of 2 12's inside and place them firing towards a big foam block and tell me the bass isn't reduced horribly. There is no way those 12's can be doing any good besides just giving you an nice back massage.<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Energy in the universe cannot be created nor destroyes, this goes for wave energy as well.  When a wave changes medium, ex: hits a more dense material at an angle less than the critical angle of internal refraction, the wave passes through the material only changing velocity, NOT frequency or amplitude.  When the wave leaves the material, the wave is partially refracted and reflected at incedent angle.  the refracted wave then returns to it's original velocity. No change in amplitude, or frequency.  This does not apply to a wave leaving the body of a vihecle as the metal absorbs energy to produce vibration (Dampening) the wave.  the reflected wave from the foam returns to the speaker and passes through (not-effecting) other waves.  I have never tested this using 2 12's and pointing them at a block of foam, but what will say is, you must be standing directly in line with the foam and the speaker.  Otherwise you are hearing the reflected wave and not the original wave.<P>You are welcome to disagree with me if you like, but I can honestly tell you that there is NO difference in sound when the seats are in the forward position, or when they are pressed against the sub.<P>Also, If all of your subs are not on the same plane facing in a similer direction, some frequencies will constructivly interfere with each other and some frequencies will de-constructivly interfere with each other.  Causing some bass notes to sound very loud and some to sound very week.<P>Even if there is no Fire Wall, there is still a substantial loss of energy when a sub is in a seperate compartment from the driver usually in the form of vibration of the trunk lid.<p>[This message has been edited by Gasolene (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||MachineHead||02-16-2001||05:10 PM||||first, your website is terribly slow.  I have cable and it feels like I'm on 56K.<P>Your wave theory doesn't work out like you say.  It doesn't come out of the seat as perfectly as you say.  The seat does absorb some of the energy, just like sound dampening.  if you don't believe me, have your car metered with the seats up and then down.  I've done simiiar installs in trucks, where the subs are against the seats.  It does change the sound, but not as much as some people say.  Also, what the hell kind of subs are those.  If you are listed max power instead of RMS, they gotta be cheap ass knock offs.  That Kenwood amp is about 2 generations old, as is that HU. ||||reg||13
Z||000028||Gasolene||02-16-2001||06:39 PM||||My site is slow because of the geocities server, not my fault.  sometimes fast, other times slow. (I may be switching hosts)<P>yes, there is some wave energy loss in the seat,  I'm sure a sensitive electronic meter would show some difference, but not enough to notice with human ears.  THATS ALL I'M GOING TO SAY ON THIS ISSUE!<P>And yes the kenwood amps are a few years old, thanks for pointing that out.  The HU is 2 years old, subs 3years.  If I were a millionare, I would be driving a Ferarie instead of a Fiero.  If you want to buy me all brand new amps, HU and subs, please do.  otherwise quit knocking my stereo. It's easy to sit at your computer and point out all the little flaws.<P>The subs are Pioneer Premier Bullets 200W Nominal 800W Peak.  $400 each, 3years ago.<BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club<p>[This message has been edited by Gasolene (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000029||sqoach||02-16-2001||07:55 PM||||yeah guys. give him a break. i realized i commented about it, but there's no need to get anything started here. eventhough his first post was saying, come check out my stereo install, that's ok. some of us don't like it, me included, but he fells a great sense of accomplishment here. i'm sure it was no easy task to build those boxes and set it all up. let's just keep our cool.<P>of course, $400 a piece??? that's a little crazy! is that canadian price??||||reg||1
Z||000030||Gasolene||02-16-2001||08:02 PM||||with GST just under $400 in summer of 97<BR>Hu was $550 summer 98, sinse then, I've been in school, and havn't had any money to purchase anything new.<BR>International stereo, Canadian prices<p>[This message has been edited by Gasolene (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000031||MachineHead||02-17-2001||03:00 PM||||Sorry for knocking you.  I'm having a fight mith my GF, and anyone who gets near me is a target.  But i still don't agree with you on the seat thing, because I have heard a difference.||||reg||1
Z||000032||Gasolene||02-17-2001||03:53 PM||||No problem.<P>I have a new site on AngleFire (same thing, just different server).  It should be alot faster.  And older netscape users CAN see it with no java errors.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ab4/fierostereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ab4/fierostereo/index.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_stereo/thumbsig.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ab4/fierostereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>My Web Page</A><BR>Edmonton Fiero Club||||reg||1
